1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:03,040
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,460
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

3
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:08,380
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

4
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:10,000
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,340
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

6
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:14,680
<i>Across this land</i>

7
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:17,010
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

8
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:19,470
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

9
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:31,780
<i>The story ends</i>

10
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:34,280
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

11
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:37,110
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

12
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:38,780
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

13
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:41,290
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

14
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:43,450
<i>Makes people forget</i>

15
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:46,250
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

16
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:48,040
<i>Begin to rust</i>

17
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:49,880
<i>Just the same</i>

18
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,170
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

19
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:55,510
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

20
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:57,380
<i>And they live on</i>

21
00:00:58,180 --> 00:00:59,930
<i>We chose the same path</i>

22
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:02,060
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

23
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:03,600
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

24
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:07,850
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

25
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:09,230
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

26
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:10,310
<i>Even now</i>

27
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:12,690
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

28
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:16,240
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

29
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:17,910
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

30
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:49,970
Ms. Frieren is falling asleep.

31
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:52,520
What?

32
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:00,840
She's asleep.

33
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:03,180
Oh, well. I'll carry her.

34
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:05,650
But Mr. Stark, your axe...

35
00:02:05,650 --> 00:02:06,880
Oh, right.

36
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:09,790
My hands are free, though.

37
00:02:19,390 --> 00:02:21,000
I'll carry her.

38
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,340
What? Why?

39
00:02:22,690 --> 00:02:23,950
No reason.

40
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:38,060
In the end, the king only
gave us ten copper coins.

41
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,530
What a cheapskate.

42
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:41,270
I'm not surprised.

43
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:46,690
Many heroes have tried and failed
to defeat the Demon King until now.

44
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:50,320
There's nothing wrong with
earning money to cover expenses

45
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:52,520
while working toward
defeating the Demon King.

46
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:56,570
It'll feel like an adventure.

47
00:02:56,570 --> 00:02:57,760
I suppose you're right.

48
00:02:58,090 --> 00:03:01,270
That's the Hero's Sword.

49
00:03:01,270 --> 00:03:02,760
It's a replica.

50
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:07,820
Back in the day, a merchant who
visited my town gave it to me

51
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:09,680
for saving him from a monster.

52
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,690
"For the future hero," he said.

53
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:14,050
Just something you'd say to a kid.

54
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:16,400
Is that why you became a hero?

55
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,310
No.

56
00:03:17,610 --> 00:03:21,270
There was this annoying brat named
Heiter at the village orphanage.

57
00:03:21,270 --> 00:03:26,790
He said I'd only ever become a fake hero
because all I had was a fake sword.

58
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:32,200
So I decided I'd prove him wrong
by becoming a real hero.

59
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:39,920
Someday, I'll acquire the real Hero's Sword
and defeat the Demon King.

60
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:44,210
But the passage of time is cruel.

61
00:03:44,630 --> 00:03:50,070
The brat who said that to me is now
a fake priest who just drinks all the time.

62
00:03:50,070 --> 00:03:51,810
I'm a real priest.

63
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:13,300
A dream...

64
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:17,140
Ms. Frieren, you're finally awake.

65
00:04:18,010 --> 00:04:20,560
I feel like I've seen this sight before.

66
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:22,990
I must still be dreaming.

67
00:04:22,990 --> 00:04:25,040
If only you were.

68
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,610
I underestimated the mountain weather.

69
00:04:27,610 --> 00:04:31,740
Keep going north. The village
we're heading to is up ahead.

70
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:32,890
Very well.

71
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:36,520
Ms. Frieren, can you walk?

72
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:38,950
No.

73
00:04:38,950 --> 00:04:40,140
I see.

74
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,010
You smell nice.

75
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:45,520
Sheesh.

76
00:04:45,770 --> 00:04:49,170
You must be tired from carrying
her this whole time, Fern.

77
00:04:49,170 --> 00:04:50,150
I'll take her now.

78
00:05:00,410 --> 00:05:01,430
Perv.

79
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,160
How am I a perv?

80
00:05:08,930 --> 00:05:11,460
The blizzard has mostly settled down.

81
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:13,440
I thought we'd freeze to death.

82
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:20,990
There really is a village this
deep in the mountains, huh?

83
00:05:23,570 --> 00:05:26,680
We've been waiting for you, Ms. Frieren.

84
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:30,860
You're the current village chief?
You're so young.

85
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:35,210
Yes. I'm the 49th in a long line of chiefs.

86
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:38,610
Welcome to the Village of the Sword.

87
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:43,080
There was a destroyed cabin
outside the village.

88
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:46,170
It's an old hunting cabin.

89
00:05:46,610 --> 00:05:48,570
The lord of the mountains destroyed it.

90
00:05:48,570 --> 00:05:51,960
The lord of the mountains?
Has there always been one of those?

91
00:05:52,370 --> 00:05:54,900
So this is the Village of the Sword.

92
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:57,340
You know of this place, Mr. Stark?

93
00:05:57,730 --> 00:06:00,320
This village used to protect the Hero's Sword.

94
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:07,740
The Hero's Sword was said to have been
placed in a sanctuary near this village.

95
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:13,730
Throughout history, many heroes tried to
pull it from the stone, but it wouldn't budge.

96
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:16,280
Not until eighty years ago, anyway.

97
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:21,750
According to the legend, uh...

98
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:24,760
"The Hero's Sword can only
be pulled from the stone

99
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:28,980
by the hero who will drive off the great
calamity bent on destroying this world."

100
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,010
Yeah, that's it.

101
00:06:30,210 --> 00:06:33,930
And it was Mr. Himmel who
drew the sword from the stone?

102
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:37,430
That's right. I thought it was
a pretty famous story.

103
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:38,760
You hadn't heard it before?

104
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:41,960
No. Mr. Heiter never mentioned it.

105
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:45,830
This is it.

106
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:49,540
So warm.

107
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,170
Anyway, I'm disappointed, Ms. Frieren.

108
00:06:53,170 --> 00:06:56,710
You were supposed to return
half a century later.

109
00:06:56,710 --> 00:07:00,090
I'm a mild-mannered person,
but even I'm pissed off.

110
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:05,160
At least, that's what my grandmother said.

111
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:08,970
I told her eighty years would be fine.

112
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:13,400
The people of this village, who've protected
the Hero's Sword for generations,

113
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:15,610
can easily defend themselves.

114
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:20,550
That's true, but we still
need you to fulfill your duty.

115
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:23,040
What duty?

116
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,680
Monster extermination.

117
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:28,440
Monsters regularly appear around this village.

118
00:07:28,730 --> 00:07:32,830
The lord of the mountain has been especially
unruly lately. It's been a real problem.

119
00:07:34,270 --> 00:07:36,680
Then I'll start tomorrow.

120
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:39,400
Better to deal with this
sooner rather than later.

121
00:07:57,050 --> 00:08:00,060
This area is full of monsters,
even though the village is nearby.

122
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:05,330
Why didn't you hire other
adventurers to exterminate them?

123
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:08,190
I wish we could, but...

124
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:10,620
It's because Himmel is the hero.

125
00:08:11,910 --> 00:08:14,690
You weren't kidding.
There sure are a lot of monsters.

126
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:18,080
They're gathered in front of that cave.

127
00:08:37,550 --> 00:08:39,420
Frieren, is this—

128
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:48,600
It's the lord.

129
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,490
I see.

130
00:08:53,490 --> 00:08:57,120
No wonder I didn't know who she meant.
It's a new face.

131
00:08:57,550 --> 00:08:59,880
Only eighty years, and you
consider yourself a lord?

132
00:09:02,370 --> 00:09:04,960
Stark, I know you can keep moving.

133
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:13,580
Can't you treat people better?

134
00:09:19,950 --> 00:09:21,220
Nice work.

135
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:32,520
Now I've fulfilled my duty.

136
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:40,250
Frieren, what's the meaning of this?

137
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:43,610
That's the Hero's Sword.

138
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:48,570
It's what attracts all the monsters.

139
00:09:48,570 --> 00:09:51,710
A powerful barrier prevents them
from entering the sanctuary,

140
00:09:51,710 --> 00:09:54,870
but even so, they can't suppress
their impulse to destroy it.

141
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:58,030
The Hero's Sword must truly terrify them.

142
00:09:58,030 --> 00:10:00,000
That's not what I meant.

143
00:10:00,610 --> 00:10:01,870
Right.

144
00:10:06,110 --> 00:10:10,150
Himmel failed to pull
the sword from the stone.

145
00:10:11,350 --> 00:10:15,280
So this hero wasn't the real one either.

146
00:10:18,010 --> 00:10:19,280
Himmel...

147
00:10:19,810 --> 00:10:22,900
There's nothing wrong
with being a fake hero.

148
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:28,050
I'll defeat the Demon King
and bring peace to the world.

149
00:10:29,850 --> 00:10:34,410
Then it won't matter if I'm fake or not.

150
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:40,330
Himmel lived up to those words.

151
00:10:40,330 --> 00:10:43,500
Even without that sword, he saved the world.

152
00:10:43,850 --> 00:10:45,480
He was a real hero.

153
00:10:46,130 --> 00:10:49,860
Then why was the truth covered up?

154
00:10:49,860 --> 00:10:53,440
It was probably done by people who
wanted to make Himmel a hero.

155
00:10:54,170 --> 00:10:56,850
No hero needs embarrassing
stories told about them,

156
00:10:56,850 --> 00:10:59,930
like the time they failed to pull
the Hero's Sword from its stone.

157
00:11:01,250 --> 00:11:06,700
Future generations always
romanticize heroes,

158
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:14,910
to the point that their original
nature eventually disappears.

159
00:11:31,750 --> 00:11:35,130
I always believed you
could do it, Ms. Frieren.

160
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:36,510
I'm hella grateful.

161
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:39,220
My grandmother said that as well.

162
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:42,370
What's up with the words
your grandma left you?

163
00:11:42,730 --> 00:11:45,230
Well, see you in another fifty years.

164
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:50,250
Don't be late next time.

165
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,300
Once we leave our belongings at the inn,

166
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:03,190
everyone's free to do what
they want for the evening.

167
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:04,870
We haven't been to a town in a while.

168
00:12:04,870 --> 00:12:06,290
We can finally cut loose.

169
00:12:07,550 --> 00:12:09,560
Ms. Frieren, what will you do?

170
00:12:09,970 --> 00:12:12,290
Shall we look around the shops together?

171
00:12:12,290 --> 00:12:13,690
I'll pass.

172
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:16,150
I'd like to relax here at the inn
and read some grimoires.

173
00:12:16,150 --> 00:12:19,200
I see. In that case, I'll go alone.

174
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,820
Oh, right.

175
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:24,290
Today is Stark's eighteenth birthday.

176
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:30,420
Why didn't you tell me that beforehand?

177
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:33,200
I didn't get him anything.

178
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:35,160
You can buy something for him in town.

179
00:12:36,770 --> 00:12:39,680
I don't know what Mr. Stark wants.

180
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:43,480
You don't think things through, do you, Fern?

181
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:45,630
This is your fault, Ms. Frieren.

182
00:12:47,090 --> 00:12:51,420
By the way, what are you giving him?

183
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:00,560
I've got something special planned.

184
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,580
A potion that only dissolves clothing.

185
00:13:08,830 --> 00:13:14,610
My master told me men enjoy
receiving this kind of gift.

186
00:13:20,690 --> 00:13:23,250
What? Are you curious, Fern?

187
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:33,130
I told you to return this vulgar
potion when you bought it.

188
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:36,420
I can't believe you, Ms. Frieren.

189
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:41,150
That potion was pretty valuable, you know.

190
00:13:42,130 --> 00:13:44,610
What am I going to give him now?

191
00:13:59,290 --> 00:14:00,130
Oh, right.

192
00:14:02,390 --> 00:14:03,930
I have this.

193
00:14:06,370 --> 00:14:09,500
<i>I'll have to look into it myself.</i>

194
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,890
<i>He's bound to notice, though.</i>

195
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:15,570
Mr. Stark.

196
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:22,600
Is he out?

197
00:14:25,950 --> 00:14:28,650
A warrior carrying an axe?

198
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:31,730
He helped me push my cart.

199
00:14:31,730 --> 00:14:34,380
I think he was headed toward the plaza.

200
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:39,290
He was playing with us until a moment ago.

201
00:14:40,890 --> 00:14:44,250
He helped us out of that tree.

202
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:48,320
He stopped my rampaging cow.

203
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:51,780
<i>He's been helping lots of people.</i>

204
00:14:53,390 --> 00:14:55,950
<i>How could Ms. Frieren be so rude?</i>

205
00:14:55,950 --> 00:15:00,260
<i>There's no way Mr. Stark would
appreciate that dirty potion.</i>

206
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:19,280
Mr. Stark.

207
00:15:18,610 --> 00:15:19,280
Whoa!

208
00:15:20,770 --> 00:15:23,590
That cloud looks like boobs.

209
00:15:25,170 --> 00:15:26,920
<i>He's a perv after all.</i>

210
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:30,810
For real? That one looks like a turd.

211
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,630
<i>No, he's just a child.</i>

212
00:15:35,630 --> 00:15:37,940
I'll have to tell Fern about them later.

213
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:40,100
<i>How am I supposed to respond to that?</i>

214
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:46,050
Mr. Stark.

215
00:15:47,490 --> 00:15:51,800
Fern, good timing. Those clouds...

216
00:15:53,990 --> 00:15:56,670
Actually, sorry. It's nothing.

217
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:00,700
Uh, so...

218
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:02,550
Would you like to go for a walk?

219
00:16:02,550 --> 00:16:03,310
Yes.

220
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:09,160
Hey, why are you mad? Did I do something?

221
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:13,380
<i>How do I broach the subject?</i>

222
00:16:14,630 --> 00:16:16,920
Come on. I'll apologize, okay?

223
00:16:17,370 --> 00:16:19,770
<i>No matter how I ask,
he'll know something's up.</i>

224
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,670
<i>Then I'll just come out and say it.</i>

225
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:27,530
Mr. Stark, is there anything you want?

226
00:16:27,530 --> 00:16:28,720
What for?

227
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:32,160
It's your birthday today.

228
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:33,910
Is that right?

229
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:36,280
What's that got to do with what I want?

230
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:41,290
I'd like to get you a birthday present.

231
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:43,410
What? You're gonna give me something?

232
00:16:44,530 --> 00:16:47,450
Actually, never mind.
You're kind of irritating.

233
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:52,920
Wait. I wasn't joking.

234
00:16:53,270 --> 00:16:56,970
I've never received a birthday present before.

235
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:06,110
I never got one from my
dead family or my master,

236
00:17:06,110 --> 00:17:08,180
so I just thought that was how it was.

237
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:10,910
Not even from your family?

238
00:17:11,450 --> 00:17:13,560
Was it not the custom there?

239
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:18,240
No, they probably just didn't
care about me that much.

240
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:22,050
I'm originally from a village of warriors.

241
00:17:22,610 --> 00:17:24,840
There was no place there for the weak.

242
00:17:25,890 --> 00:17:28,270
That was a pathetic display
in front of that monster.

243
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:30,420
Try to be more like Stoltz.

244
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:34,800
Not only is he uninjured, but he doesn't
have a speck of blood or dirt on him.

245
00:17:37,420 --> 00:17:42,300
His pure white cape proves he's
the strongest warrior in the village.

246
00:17:42,670 --> 00:17:44,910
Stoltz, you're the pride of the village.

247
00:17:44,910 --> 00:17:46,540
Of course, Dad.

248
00:17:50,140 --> 00:17:53,860
But by contrast, Stark is a failure.

249
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:59,830
Despite training so hard every day,
he still hasn't faced down a monster.

250
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:06,000
It's starting to rain. Let's head home.

251
00:18:06,590 --> 00:18:08,840
I'm going to train my
foolish younger brother.

252
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:10,860
Don't be too mean to him.

253
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:13,580
I'm heading home. You're wasting your time.

254
00:18:17,090 --> 00:18:18,220
Stark.

255
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:24,590
Brother.

256
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:29,360
Sorry.

257
00:18:30,490 --> 00:18:32,470
Good focus.

258
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:38,860
I know you'll become stronger, but your
stance could use some improvement.

259
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:45,640
Come to think of it, my brother
might've been different.

260
00:18:46,570 --> 00:18:47,470
But...

261
00:18:56,200 --> 00:19:01,810
When my village was attacked by monsters,
I abandoned even my brother and fled.

262
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,690
Maybe I shouldn't be surprised my family
never celebrated my birthday.

263
00:19:06,150 --> 00:19:08,430
I was a failure who ran from everything.

264
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:13,600
I bet Himmel wouldn't have run.

265
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:22,210
Mr. Stark, let's go pick out a present.

266
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:26,220
The past doesn't matter.

267
00:19:26,830 --> 00:19:31,340
The warrior Stark I've known has never run.

268
00:19:32,370 --> 00:19:34,830
But I might in the future.

269
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:36,970
We won't let you.

270
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:38,830
But I—

271
00:19:38,830 --> 00:19:41,580
If you won't choose, then I'm
choosing something for you.

272
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:45,720
Fine.

273
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,650
I'd like this, then.

274
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,740
No. That's expensive.

275
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:54,530
Okay.

276
00:20:03,550 --> 00:20:05,750
Welcome back. You're late.

277
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:10,560
Ms. Frieren, what are those
ridiculously large hamburg steaks?

278
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:12,250
What are you talking about?

279
00:20:12,250 --> 00:20:14,370
This is how you celebrate a birthday.

280
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,860
My master never gave me any gifts,

281
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:20,630
but he did make me birthday hamburg steaks.

282
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,740
What do you mean?

283
00:20:22,740 --> 00:20:26,050
Stark, Eisen didn't tell you?

284
00:20:26,050 --> 00:20:26,900
Tell me what?

285
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:30,460
Warriors are so awkward.

286
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:32,890
You're one to talk, aren't you, Ms. Frieren?

287
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:36,680
You're right. I understand
because I'm awkward, too.

288
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:38,100
It's foolish, isn't it?

289
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:41,500
People won't know how you feel
unless you tell them.

290
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:43,560
This is...

291
00:20:46,210 --> 00:20:47,560
Come to think of it,

292
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:51,830
you always make ridiculously large
hamburg steaks on our birthdays.

293
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:52,840
What's that about?

294
00:20:53,140 --> 00:20:56,070
It's a custom in my region.

295
00:20:56,070 --> 00:21:00,700
They're a gift to honor warriors
who have worked hard.

296
00:21:01,130 --> 00:21:04,860
It's like a birthday present from me.

297
00:21:04,860 --> 00:21:08,100
But Eisen, we're not warriors.

298
00:21:08,430 --> 00:21:11,610
Everyone who works hard is a warrior.

299
00:21:11,610 --> 00:21:12,930
Really?

300
00:21:12,930 --> 00:21:14,290
Who can say?

301
00:21:14,990 --> 00:21:18,000
Warriors who have worked hard...

302
00:21:18,710 --> 00:21:21,130
Brother, what are you making?

303
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:24,570
Hamburg steak. It's your birthday, isn't it?

304
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:27,350
Don't tell the rest of the family.

305
00:21:34,570 --> 00:21:36,120
Run, Stark.

306
00:21:38,850 --> 00:21:40,410
You have to live.

307
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:12,420
Eisen gave me the recipe.

308
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:15,020
Is it good?

309
00:22:23,290 --> 00:22:24,150
Yeah.

310
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:32,220
I have some of this left over, too.

311
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:35,170
I'll pour it over your
head again, Ms. Frieren.

312
00:22:35,170 --> 00:22:37,340
Huh? What's that?

313
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:39,690
None of your business.

314
00:22:39,690 --> 00:22:41,470
A valuable potion.

315
00:22:41,470 --> 00:22:43,090
What? What's it do?

316
00:22:43,090 --> 00:22:44,260
Perv.

317
00:22:44,260 --> 00:22:45,700
What? How am I a perv?

318
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:46,650
Perv.

319
00:22:46,650 --> 00:22:48,900
Seriously, why?

320
00:22:50,070 --> 00:22:52,620
<i>And you alright</i>

321
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,120
<i>Can you hear me</i>

322
00:22:55,910 --> 00:23:02,000
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

323
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,340
<i>Crying excessively</i>

324
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:07,510
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

325
00:23:07,510 --> 00:23:13,550
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

326
00:23:13,550 --> 00:23:17,270
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

327
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:20,020
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

328
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:25,690
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

329
00:23:25,690 --> 00:23:29,240
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

330
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:32,280
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

331
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:37,040
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

332
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:43,130
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

333
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:48,960
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

334
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:54,970
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

335
00:23:54,970 --> 00:24:00,730
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

336
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:03,690
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

337
00:24:03,690 --> 00:24:06,610
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

338
00:24:06,610 --> 00:24:12,780
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

339
00:24:12,780 --> 00:24:15,450
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

340
00:24:15,450 --> 00:24:19,370
<i>for you to come back home</i>

341
00:24:20,290 --> 00:24:21,700
Himmel!

342
00:24:20,970 --> 00:24:22,710
My nose is starting to bleed.

343
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:23,460
You're a wicked woman.

344
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:23,690
Alcohol is the best medicine.

345
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:24,460
So what, Frieren?

346
00:24:23,690 --> 00:24:26,660
Too much time has passed.
Nothing that can be done now.

347
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:25,650
Grown-ups are dirty.

348
00:24:24,690 --> 00:24:27,230
He also likes older women.

349
00:24:27,230 --> 00:24:30,060
It's an aversion to my own kind, I guess.
